## Summary

Closes pnpm/pnpm#16502
Closes pnpm/pnpm#15567

`pnpm setup` and `pnpm self-update` install the CLI as the package `pnpm`, and the bin linker writes no `pnpm.ps1` for it, so PowerShell and cmd.exe both run `pnpm.cmd`. That shim ran `pnpm.exe` as a batch job, and when Ctrl+C stopped a script, cmd.exe asked `Terminate batch job (Y/N)?` after `pnpm.exe` exited. The `script-shell` setting had nothing to do with it.

The `.cmd` shims of the pnpm CLI (packages `pnpm` and `@pnpm/exe`, the set `wants_powershell_shim` already opts out) now end their batch context before `pnpm.exe` starts:

```bat
@SETLOCAL
@SET "_PNPM_RESTORE_TITLE="
@SETLOCAL EnableDelayedExpansion
@SET "_PNPM_CMDLINE=!CMDCMDLINE:/c=!"
@IF "!_PNPM_CMDLINE!"=="!CMDCMDLINE!" (ENDLOCAL & SET "_PNPM_RESTORE_TITLE=1") ELSE ENDLOCAL
@GOTO #_undefined_# 2>NUL || (IF "%_PNPM_RESTORE_TITLE%"=="1" TITLE %COMSPEC%) & "%~dp0\..\global\v11\<hash>\node_modules\pnpm\pnpm.exe"  %*
```

- The `GOTO` to a missing label ends the batch context. cmd.exe still runs the rest of the parsed line, in command-line context, with `%~dp0` and `%*` already expanded.
- Interactive cmd.exe appends the batch command to the window title and restores it when the batch ends. This exit skips the restore, so without a fix the title grows with every call (measured). npm's cmd-shim always runs `title %COMSPEC%` for this. That also sets the PowerShell window title to `cmd.exe` for the whole `pnpm dev` run (measured), so this shim resets the title 
